From: MakOS Project <makos@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] widget/makos: show the native top-level on creation

MakOS owns one browser top-level surface slot and does not have a separate
window-manager show handshake. Make that native surface visible immediately
after successful creation. This queues the normal Gecko invalidation and
paint path while keeping a later Firefox Show(true) idempotent.

diff --git a/widget/makos/MakOSWindow.cpp b/widget/makos/MakOSWindow.cpp
--- a/widget/makos/MakOSWindow.cpp
+++ b/widget/makos/MakOSWindow.cpp
@@ -189,6 +189,10 @@ class MakOSWindow final : public HeadlessWidget {
     gTopLevelWindow = this;
     makos::FillSurface(mSurface, 0xfff0f0f0, 0, 0, rect.Width(),
                        rect.Height());
+    // MakOS owns the browser's single native top-level slot. Make it visible
+    // as soon as creation succeeds so frontend service initialization cannot
+    // indefinitely defer the first real Gecko paint.
+    Show(true);
     return NS_OK;
   }
 
